Subject: feat(model-popover,test): add data-action=provider-connect to "+" IconButton (G5.1)

G5.1 staged the dialog-select-provider interaction test, but the
provider dialog has no stable trigger anchor reachable from a session:
the only in-session path is the "+" IconButton inside the model
popover, which has aria-label but no data-action (and the settings
"View all" button / provider.connect command require opening the
settings dialog first).

Add `data-action="provider-connect"` to the "+" IconButton in
dialog-select-model's ModelSelectorPopover so the surfaces test can
drive the flow via a stable selector (the model popover is already
reachable via [data-action="prompt-model"]).

Dialog presence is asserted by querying the Kobalte dialog title text
(`language.t("command.provider.connect")`) which is unique to this
dialog — no additional product-side signal required.

Once this lands, tests-gui/tests/surfaces/test_dialogs_group_a.py::
test_dialog_select_provider_opens_and_closes drops its xfail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/packages/app/src/components/dialog-select-model.tsx b/packages/app/src/components/dialog-select-model.tsx
--- a/packages/app/src/components/dialog-select-model.tsx
+++ b/packages/app/src/components/dialog-select-model.tsx
@@ -171,6 +171,7 @@ export function ModelSelectorPopover(props: {
                 <Tooltip placement="top" value={language.t("command.provider.connect")}>
                   <IconButton
                     icon="plus-small"
+                    data-action="provider-connect"
                     variant="ghost"
                     iconSize="normal"
                     class="size-6"
